    "result_text": "The build is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` with all derived values moved onto that new identity.\n\n**New utility** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../util/Sha256Hex.java`: `upperHexPrefix(input, length)` returns the first N upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of the input.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1`**:\n- Replaced the sequence-based `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` with `customerCode(owner)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - `REGION` = `LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode)` (the region derived from the postcode, falling back to the city).\n  - `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n- The sequence number is gone entirely (`countOwnersInCity` remains, still used by the per-city capacity check).\n- The **membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), **check digit** (Luhn over the customer code's digits, via the mapper), and the **create audit record** all consume the customer code verbatim, so they now carry the region-and-hash identity automatically. Verified in the run: `AUDIT - Owner created: ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`**: the **locality** derivation now reads the `REGION` segment of the customer code (the part before the first `-`), falling back to `LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode)` when an owner has no customer code (e.g. seed data) \u2014 so locality is now derived from the new identity rather than independently.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to document the new format.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) passes, and the full suite is green.\n\nNote: `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` and `membership_number VARCHAR(20)` comfortably fit the new values (max region `UNKNOWN` \u2192 `UNKNOWN-XXXXXXXX` = 16 chars; membership `+-M26` = 20 chars).",
